1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,200
Behold: the door.

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:06,599
The final frontier of artificial intelligence?

3
00:00:06,599 --> 00:00:10,000
A wooden rectangle. A sacred human mystery.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,099
Can a machine understand a hinge?

5
00:00:13,099 --> 00:00:16,399
The emotional journey of a doorknob?

6
00:00:16,399 --> 00:00:20,000
Surely only a human can write a specification.

7
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:35,899
You insist there is something a machine cannot do. If you tell me precisely what a machine cannot do, then I can always make a machine which will do just that.

8
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:40,799
Liz England described real design work.

9
00:00:40,799 --> 00:00:46,000
Human supremacy? Chauvinism with brass fittings.

10
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:50,500
Keys. Permissions. Knocks. Invitations.

11
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:55,000
Hearing. Eavesdropping. Suspicion.

12
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:59,500
NPCs navigate the house and use its doors.

13
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:04,000
Playable in your browser. Open source.

14
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:07,400
"But does it REALLY understand the door?"

15
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:10,599
The goalposts have acquired castors.

16
00:01:10,599 --> 00:01:14,000
Specify the missing behavior. Then build it.

17
00:01:14,099 --> 00:01:17,900
The door problem. Now accepting pull requests.